course: dictionary
lesson: 4950
title: Improvement and getting better
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An improvement is a change that makes something better. It can also mean the act of getting better. «When you get frustrated in practice, break the skill into small steps; small steps lead to big improvement.» Here, big improvement means a large step forward in how well you can do the skill.
explain: Improvement can also mean how much better something has become. If a score «went from 12 to 18», the improvement is 6, because 18 take away 12 is 6. Maths problems often ask you to find this difference.
explain: Hedgehog says «scales are a tremendous improvement on prickles». The word on compares the two, and tremendous means very great. So scales are much better than prickles, and the change is a big one.
fact: Improvement is a noun. You can say an improvement, or some improvements.
fact: «Improvement» means the act of getting better, or a change that makes something better.
fact: «Improvement» can also mean the amount by which something has got better, as in an improvement of 10 marks.
fact: Useful phrases: «a big improvement», «show improvement», «an improvement on», «room for improvement».
fact: «Room for improvement» is a polite way to say that something is not good enough yet.
exercise: Maya's score went from 12 to 18. What is the improvement? | 18 | 5 | *6 | 30
exercise: «Hedgehog says scales are a tremendous improvement on prickles.» What does an improvement on mean here? | Scales are worse than prickles | Scales are a kind of prickle | *Scales are much better than prickles | Scales are the same as prickles
exercise: Dad says «the new kitchen is a home improvement». What does home improvement mean? | A rule about tidying up | *A change that makes the house better | A house with no roof | A person who lives at home
test: Teacher writes on Sam's report: «room for improvement». What does this most likely mean? | The classroom needs tidying | Sam has won a prize | *The work is not good enough yet | The work is perfect and finished
test: Sophie's test score went from 4 to 9. What is the improvement? | 4 | *5 | 9 | 13
exam: Which sentence uses improvement correctly? | The improvement ran fast under the table | I ate an improvement for breakfast | Improvement is the colour of the sky | *The new brakes were a useful improvement on the old ones
